## Plugin Configuration Best Practices

### Environment-Based Configuration
```javascript
// ✅ USE environment variables for plugin config
const pool = new Pool({
  host: process.env.DB_HOST,
  port: process.env.DB_PORT,
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
  user: process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD
});

// ❌ AVOID hardcoded configuration
const pool = new Pool({
  host: 'localhost',
  port: 5432,
  database: 'slam25_db'
});
```

### Plugin-Specific Configuration Files
```javascript
// ✅ USE dedicated config files
// tailwind.config.js - TailwindCSS configuration
// vite.config.js - Vite build configuration
// jest.config.cjs - Jest testing configuration

// ❌ AVOID mixing configurations
// config.js - All configurations in one file
```

## Remember: Always check package.json first, then use established patterns before implementing custom solutions.